  "id": "Compound::DB06201 - Gene::6332",
  "verbalization": "Rufinamide appears to interact with voltage-gated sodium channels through a shared mechanism involving participation in sodium channel activity. The evidence suggests that Rufinamide binds to multiple sodium channel subunits—Scn11a, Scn4a, and Scn2a—each of which participates in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This activity is then linked to Scn7a, indicating a potential role for Rufinamide in modulating sodium channel function in Scn7a. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with the shared involvement of voltage-gated sodium channels as a critical intermediary. The mechanism appears to rely on the binding of Rufinamide to different subunits of the same family of sodium channels, which in turn influence Scn7a's function. This suggests that Rufinamide may act through a common pathway involving sodium channel activity, potentially affecting the function of Scn7a in a broader physiological context.",
